{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS CloudTrail adds data event aggregation to simplify security monitoring - AWS","context":"AWS CloudTrail, a service that records API calls for AWS account activity, introduces a new feature called CloudTrail aggregated events. This feature simplifies monitoring and analysis of high-volume CloudTrail data events by consolidating them into 5-minute summaries. Security, compliance, and operations teams can efficiently identify trends like access frequency, error rates, and frequently used actions without processing individual events. Aggregations are available for API activity, resource access, and user activity summaries. Users can enable aggregation through the AWS console or CLI and choose from pre-built templates. The aggregation service is charged based on the number of CloudTrail data events analyzed. It is available in all commercial AWS Regions. With this feature, teams can answer questions like \"How has this user's activity changed over the past week?\" or \"What are the top actions being performed on this critical resource?\" without having to scan through massive amounts of CloudTrail data events","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/cloudtrail-data-event-aggregation-security-monitoring/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region","skill_description":"Enables a multi-region AWS CloudTrail trail with S3 log storage, CloudWatch Logs integration, and CloudWatch Logs Insights queries for security monitoring and compliance auditing. Use when setting up centralized API activity logging across all AWS regions.\n\nServices: cloudtrail, s3, cloudwatch, iam, kms\nTasks: configure, secure, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: security, monitoring\n*","skill_name":"setting-up-cloudtrail-multi-region"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"aws-investigation","skill_description":"Investigates what is happening in an AWS account from evidence already recorded there. Not for capturing new data from running code (snapshots of function arguments on a live service, Dynamic Instrumentation), questions answered from the CloudWatch Omni context graph or Application Signals service map, or building or changing infrastructure. Covers reading deployment records instead of the newest stored version (completed AppConfig deployments, the version an alias points to, a stack's current template), following a request through every service's own logs (exact per-layer fields, unique failed requests in an alarm's breach window, failure boundary per event), and answering questions from the account's data (exact counts and breakdowns, coverage of the requested range, exact filters and joins, the rule behind failed or unmatched records, verbatim values). Use to triage an alarm, error spike or failed request, trace a request across services, or count, break down, extract or join records.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, appconfig, lambda, cloudformation, dynamodb, s3, athena, glue\nTasks: debug, investigate, query, troubleshoot\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: observability, operations","skill_name":"aws-investigation"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"querying-aws-cloudwatch","skill_description":"Runs SQL queries on CloudWatch Logs data exported as Apache Iceberg tables in S3 Tables. Covers VPC Flow Logs, WAF logs, CloudFront access logs, Route 53 resolver logs, Network Firewall logs, EKS audit logs, Verified Access logs, SES logs, VPC Lattice logs, Step Functions logs, NLB access logs, S3 Server Access Logs, and 20+ other AWS vended data sources. Applies when analyzing network traffic, investigating security incidents, querying exported logs with SQL, enabling S3 Tables integration, configuring log export, correlating logs with other data, running Athena queries on the aws-cloudwatch table bucket, analyzing S3 access patterns, S3 latency investigation, S3 cost attribution, or bucket access auditing.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, s3tables, athena, glue, s3\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, audit, configure\nPersona: developer, data-engineer, devops\nWorkload: data-analytics, observability\n*","skill_name":"querying-aws-cloudwatch"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Verify AWS docs on CloudTrail Event history limitations versus trails"}
